cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite the NOVA-Mem software repository and consult
  docs/RESEARCH_STATUS.md for the S-36 experiment snapshot, including its
  documented ZAI glm-4-plus backend deviation from the frozen Ollama/Qwen
  configuration.
title: >-
  NOVA-Mem: A Resource-Aware Evaluation Framework for Conversational Memory Strategies
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/zafaraieng/nova-mem"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-20"
keywords:
  - artificial-intelligence
  - conversational-memory
  - long-term-memory
  - retrieval-augmented-generation
  - LongMemEval
  - research-software
  - python
abstract: >-
  Research software for evaluating conversational memory and retrieval
  strategies under resource constraints using the cleaned LongMemEval
  benchmark. The repository includes configurable memory-system paths,
  model adapters, retrieval and reranking components, evaluation utilities,
  experiment tracking, tests, and reproducibility documentation. Research
  status and backend deviations are documented separately.
